WEBVTT

2.1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.250
You start on Availability Requests.

2.2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.175
An availability request is us asking whether you can supply the plants for a job.

2.3
00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:15.483
Across the top are three boxes: New, Processing and Completed.

2.4
00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:22.733
New means it's waiting for you. Processing means you've started. Completed means you've sent your answers.

2.5
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.317
Tap a box to show or hide those requests.

2.6
00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:34.117
Each card shows the job, the date it's needed, pickup or delivery, the number of items and the value.

2.7
00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:41.842
On a computer, the menu sits on the left: Orders, Availability Requests, and further down, History and Settings.

2.8
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.750
On a phone, it's the bar along the bottom.

2.9
00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:52.067
The bell, called Alerts on a phone, shows new requests and replies from us.

2.10
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:57.233
We don't send emails for new requests, so the bell is the place to check.
